    {
      "id": 25,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "title": "Native use / timing / limits",
      "pos": [
        820,
        950
      ],
      "size": [
        700,
        420
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 24,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Native conditioning, with small public BFS helpers\nUpload the guide and Picture 1. The second image is disconnected and OPTIONAL; connect more native ref_images slots consecutively (up to 9) and assign their roles in the editable H3 prompt. No Planner or prompt VLM is required.\n\nSource aspect ratio sets the output; 0.4 MP cap; 24 fps; initial test limited to 107 decoded frames. To use a longer clip, change BOTH VHS frame_load_cap and Prepare max_frames. Prefer the Planner workflow for long videos and camera cuts. Padding is trimmed to the actual source duration.\n\nAudio output copies the source; no dialogue is inferred or generated. Motion/identity fidelity still needs visual review. Native means native H3 conditioning, not zero custom nodes: BFS handles source geometry (and TARA), VHS loads the video. No Henge private nodes required."
      ],
      "color": "#234",
      "bgcolor": "#345"
    },
    {
      "id": 26,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "title": "START HERE — choose the matching Motion Transfer LoRA",
      "pos": [
        0,
        1130
      ],
      "size": [
        700,
        480
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 25,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Motion Transfer v1.0 — Guide Latents / native_nodes\n\nMatching LoRA: minimax_h3_motion_transfer_v1.0_ref2va.safetensors\nTraining adapter V2 → DMD Ref2VA 8-step turbo → task LoRA; strengths 1, CFG 1, Euler/simple, 8 steps. These are inference defaults, not quality guarantees. Do not load another copy of an already merged adapter/turbo.\n\nThe guide enters through Add Guide, not native video-reference latents. Planner additionally shows sampled guide frames to the text encoder.\n\nDependencies: updated ComfyUI native MiniMax H3, ComfyUI-BFSNodes 1.115.33+, VideoHelperSuite for native video loading. Model download links are in docs/motion-transfer.md in the HF repo. Select installed model names if your files are in subfolders.\n\nThese graphs are derived from the native/Planner contracts of the published Character Swap v1.1 workflows, with Motion Transfer-specific prompts and model wiring. No bundled private media; replace guide.mp4/reference_1.png before queueing."
      ],
      "color": "#234",
      "bgcolor": "#345"
    },
    {
      "id": 27,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "title": "N reference images — read before assigning roles",
      "pos": [
        1580,
        1130
      ],
      "size": [
        680,
        520
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 26,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# References are flexible: 1..N pictures, not a person/background pair\nOnly Picture 1 is connected by default. Picture 2 is OPTIONAL and disconnected. Add consecutive slots 1..N as needed (native H3 supports up to 9); in Planner use the reference list, globally or per shot.\n\nA picture may describe a character, outfit, object, setting or style. Several pictures may describe the SAME character. Two images can be two characters, two views of one identity, or any other explicitly requested combination. A separate background is NOT required. Image count is NOT performer count.\n\nAssign the role of every attached picture in the prompt. The guide supplies motion and timing. Preserve its setting/camera unless you explicitly ask to replace them. Avoid ambiguity for multiple performers: include clothes/identity, time of entry, occlusion and back views. Inspect the generated prompt before relying on it. Prompt instructions improve binding; they do not guarantee perfect identity tracking.\n\nExamples: one identity picture; three distinct character pictures; two views of one identity plus an outfit; or character + object + setting. These are choices, not mandatory slots. No automatic background removal is applied in these examples."
      ],
      "color": "#234",
      "bgcolor": "#345"
    },
    {
      "id": 28,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "title": "Kitchen compatibility / MODIFIED TARA kernel",
      "pos": [
        2320,
        1130
      ],
      "size": [
        760,
        650
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 27,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Comfy Kitchen + TARA: supported with the MODIFIED temporal kernel\nGuide Latents can use ordinary Comfy Kitchen attention. TARA's fused one-pass Kitchen path additionally needs the modified temporal extension (library AND Python API); installing stock comfy-kitchen alone does not provide it.\n\nSafe default here: TARA uses PyTorch model attention + Flash partitions (no compile). To try Kitchen, select comfy kitchen attention in Model Attention Backend and comfy kitchen (experimental) in the TARA/conditioning backend control.\n\nUpdate BFSNodes main (1.115.33+), restart ComfyUI, then let BFS install its verified temporal extension on supported Linux/Windows x86_64 NVIDIA GPUs. CUDA-13-capable driver required; PyTorch can use CUDA 12.x. Unsupported/offline setups may keep a slower compatibility path. Flash partitions does not require this extension.\n\nConfirm the fused kernel in the sampling log: Kitchen ONE-PASS dense kernel ACTIVE (or Kitchen ONE-PASS sol kernel ACTIVE when separately using supported Sol attention). A completed render alone does not prove it used the modified kernel. Do not add VSA/SLA to these examples.\n\nSetup and limitations: https://github.com/alisson-anjos/ComfyUI-BFSNodes/blob/main/H3_NATIVE_TEMPORAL.md#kernel-downloads\nManual install: https://github.com/alisson-anjos/comfy-kitchen/blob/feat/h3-native-temporal/MANUAL_TEMPORAL_INSTALL.md\nVerified release/checksums: https://github.com/alisson-anjos/comfy-kitchen/releases/tag/temporal-native-0413d43878606425a84aa400f1e5da50ed9dcdad\nBinaries passed ABI/build checks; not every GPU/OS has full-video validation."
      ],
      "color": "#234",
      "bgcolor": "#345"
    }
